(75,'C.D_M.3.3.0.2. Teoremas para calcular la derivada de una función trigonométricas directas.','C.D_M.3.3.0.2. Teoremas para c',27,3,1,0,'<!-- TÍTULO PRINCIPAL -->\n<div style=\"background-color: #e6f0ff; border: 2px solid #3399ff; padding: 10px; text-align: center; margin-bottom: 20px;\">\n  <strong style=\"color: #0066cc;\">C.D_M.3.3.0.5. TEOREMAS PARA CALCULAR LA DERIVADA DE FUNCIONES TRIGONOMÉTRICAS DIRECTAS</strong>\n</div>\n\n<div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: center; margin: 20px 0;\">\n  <iframe width=\"560\" height=\"315\" \n    src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/g_DKnIDJtm4\" \n    title=\"Derivadas de funciones trigonométricas | Khan Academy\" \n    frameborder=\"0\" \n    allow=\"accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share\" \n    referrerpolicy=\"strict-origin-when-cross-origin\" \n    allowfullscreen>\n  </iframe>\n</div>\n\n<!-- TEOREMA 1: f(x) = sin(x) -->\n<div style=\"background-color: #e6f0ff; padding: 15px; margin-bottom: 20px;\">\n  <p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong style=\"color: #0066cc;\">DERIVADA DE f(x) = sin(x)</strong></p>\n  <p>La derivada del seno es:</p>\n  <p style=\"text-align: center;\">\\[\\frac{d}{dx}(\\sin x) = \\cos x\\]</p>\n\n  <br>\n  <div style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Ejemplo 1:</strong></div>\n  <div style=\"text-align: center;\">\n    <p>\\[f(x) = \\sin x\\]</p>\n    <p>\\[\\frac{d}{dx}(\\sin x)\\]</p>\n    <p>\\[f\'(x) = \\cos x\\]</p>\n  </div>\n\n  <br>\n  <div style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Ejemplo 2:</strong></div>\n  <div style=\"text-align: center;\">\n    <p>\\[f(x) = 3\\sin x\\]</p>\n    <p>\\[\\frac{d}{dx}(3\\sin x)\\]</p>\n    <p>\\[f\'(x) = 3\\cos x\\]</p>\n  </div>\n</div>\n\n<!-- TEOREMA 2: f(x) = cos(x) -->\n<div style=\"background-color: #f5f5f5; padding: 15px; margin-bottom: 20px;\">\n  <p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong style=\"color: #0066cc;\">DERIVADA DE f(x) = cos(x)</strong></p>\n  <p>La derivada del coseno es:</p>\n  <p style=\"text-align: center;\">\\[\\frac{d}{dx}(\\cos x) = -\\sin x\\]</p>\n\n  <br>\n  <div style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Ejemplo 1:</strong></div>\n  <div style=\"text-align: center;\">\n    <p>\\[f(x) = \\cos x\\]</p>\n    <p>\\[\\frac{d}{dx}(\\cos x)\\]</p>\n    <p>\\[f\'(x) = -\\sin x\\]</p>\n  </div>\n\n  <br>\n  <div style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Ejemplo 2:</strong></div>\n  <div style=\"text-align: center;\">\n    <p>\\[f(x) = 4\\cos x\\]</p>\n    <p>\\[\\frac{d}{dx}(4\\cos x)\\]</p>\n    <p>\\[f\'(x) = -4\\sin x\\]</p>\n  </div>\n</div>\n\n<!-- TEOREMA 3: f(x) = tan(x) -->\n<div style=\"background-color: #e6f0ff; padding: 15px; margin-bottom: 20px;\">\n  <p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong style=\"color: #0066cc;\">DERIVADA DE f(x) = tan(x)</strong></p>\n  <p>La derivada de la tangente es:</p>\n  <p style=\"text-align: center;\">\\[\\frac{d}{dx}(\\tan x) = \\sec^2 x\\]</p>\n\n  <br>\n  <div style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Ejemplo 1:</strong></div>\n  <div style=\"text-align: center;\">\n    <p>\\[f(x) = \\tan x\\]</p>\n    <p>\\[\\frac{d}{dx}(\\tan x)\\]</p>\n    <p>\\[f\'(x) = \\sec^2 x\\]</p>\n  </div>\n\n  <br>\n  <div style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Ejemplo 2:</strong></div>\n  <div style=\"text-align: center;\">\n    <p>\\[f(x) = 2\\tan x\\]</p>\n    <p>\\[\\frac{d}{dx}(2\\tan x)\\]</p>\n    <p>\\[f\'(x) = 2\\sec^2 x\\]</p>\n  </div>\n</div>\n\n<div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: center; margin: 20px 0;\">\n  <iframe width=\"560\" height=\"315\" \n    src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/D6wURCoShA8\" \n    title=\"Derivadas de funciones trigonométricas | Video educativo\" \n    frameborder=\"0\" \n    allow=\"accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share\" \n    referrerpolicy=\"strict-origin-when-cross-origin\" \n    allowfullscreen>\n  </iframe>\n</div>\n\n\n<!-- TEOREMA 4: f(x) = cot(x) -->\n<div style=\"background-color: #f5f5f5; padding: 15px; margin-bottom: 20px;\">\n  <p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong style=\"color: #0066cc;\">DERIVADA DE f(x) = cot(x)</strong></p>\n  <p>La derivada de la cotangente es:</p>\n  <p style=\"text-align: center;\">\\[\\frac{d}{dx}(\\cot x) = -\\csc^2 x\\]</p>\n\n  <br>\n  <div style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Ejemplo 1:</strong></div>\n  <div style=\"text-align: center;\">\n    <p>\\[f(x) = \\cot x\\]</p>\n    <p>\\[\\frac{d}{dx}(\\cot x)\\]</p>\n    <p>\\[f\'(x) = -\\csc^2 x\\]</p>\n  </div>\n\n  <br>\n  <div style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Ejemplo 2:</strong></div>\n  <div style=\"text-align: center;\">\n    <p>\\[f(x) = 5\\cot x\\]</p>\n    <p>\\[\\frac{d}{dx}(5\\cot x)\\]</p>\n    <p>\\[f\'(x) = -5\\csc^2 x\\]</p>\n  </div>\n</div>\n\n<!-- TEOREMA 5: f(x) = sec(x) -->\n<div style=\"background-color: #e6f0ff; padding: 15px; margin-bottom: 20px;\">\n  <p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong style=\"color: #0066cc;\">DERIVADA DE f(x) = sec(x)</strong></p>\n  <p>La derivada de la secante es:</p>\n  <p style=\"text-align: center;\">\\[\\frac{d}{dx}(\\sec x) = \\sec x \\tan x\\]</p>\n\n  <br>\n  <div style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Ejemplo 1:</strong></div>\n  <div style=\"text-align: center;\">\n    <p>\\[f(x) = \\sec x\\]</p>\n    <p>\\[\\frac{d}{dx}(\\sec x)\\]</p>\n    <p>\\[f\'(x) = \\sec x \\tan x\\]</p>\n  </div>\n\n  <br>\n  <div style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Ejemplo 2:</strong></div>\n  <div style=\"text-align: center;\">\n    <p>\\[f(x) = 3\\sec x\\]</p>\n    <p>\\[\\frac{d}{dx}(3\\sec x)\\]</p>\n    <p>\\[f\'(x) = 3\\sec x \\tan x\\]</p>\n  </div>\n</div>\n\n<!-- TEOREMA 6: f(x) = csc(x) -->\n<div style=\"background-color: #f5f5f5; padding: 15px; margin-bottom: 20px;\">\n  <p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong style=\"color: #0066cc;\">DERIVADA DE f(x) = csc(x)</strong></p>\n  <p>La derivada de la cosecante es:</p>\n  <p style=\"text-align: center;\">\\[\\frac{d}{dx}(\\csc x) = -\\csc x \\cot x\\]</p>\n\n  <br>\n  <div style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Ejemplo 1:</strong></div>\n  <div style=\"text-align: center;\">\n    <p>\\[f(x) = \\csc x\\]</p>\n    <p>\\[\\frac{d}{dx}(\\csc x)\\]</p>\n    <p>\\[f\'(x) = -\\csc x \\cot x\\]</p>\n  </div>\n\n  <br>\n  <div style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Ejemplo 2:</strong></div>\n  <div style=\"text-align: center;\">\n    <p>\\[f(x) = 2\\csc x\\]</p>\n    <p>\\[\\frac{d}{dx}(2\\csc x)\\]</p>\n    <p>\\[f\'(x) = -2\\csc x \\cot x\\]</p>\n  </div>\n</div>\n\n<!-- REFERENCIAS -->\n<br>\n<p><strong>Referencias:</strong></p>\n<ul style=\"list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;\">\n  <li>Stewart, J. (2013). <em>Cálculo: Trascendentes tempranas</em> (7ª ed.). Cengage Learning.</li>\n  <li>Larson, R., & Hostetler, R. P. (2006). <em>Cálculo y geometría analítica</em> (8ª ed.). McGraw-Hill.</li>\n  <li>Paul’s Online Math Notes. (n.d.). <em>Calculus I – Derivatives of Trig Functions</em>. Lamar University. Recuperado de:  \n    <a href=\"https://tutorial.math.lamar.edu/Classes/CalcI/DiffTrigFunctions.aspx\" target=\"_blank\">\n      https://tutorial.math.lamar.edu/Classes/CalcI/DiffTrigFunctions.aspx\n    </a>\n  </li>\n</ul>','hybrid','','2025-04-15 15:26:40','2025-10-27 19:37:50'),
(76,'C.D_M.3.3.0.3. Teoremas para calcular la derivada de una función trigonométricas inversas.','C.D_M.3.3.0.3. Teoremas para c',27,4,1,0,'<!-- TÍTULO PRINCIPAL -->\n<div style=\"background-color: #e6f0ff; border: 2px solid #3399ff; padding: 10px; text-align: center; margin-bottom: 20px;\">\n  <strong style=\"color: #0066cc;\">C.D_M.3.3.0.6. TEOREMAS PARA CALCULAR LA DERIVADA DE FUNCIONES TRIGONOMÉTRICAS INVERSAS</strong>\n</div>\n\n<div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: center; margin: 20px 0;\">\n  <iframe width=\"560\" height=\"315\" \n    src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/5vQZyqQycUQ\" \n    title=\"Derivadas de funciones trigonométricas inversas | Khan Academy\" \n    frameborder=\"0\" \n    allow=\"accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share\" \n    referrerpolicy=\"strict-origin-when-cross-origin\" \n    allowfullscreen>\n  </iframe>\n</div>\n\n<!-- TEOREMA 1: f(x) = arcsin(x) -->\n<div style=\"background-color: #e6f0ff; padding: 15px; margin-bottom: 20px;\">\n  <p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong style=\"color: #0066cc;\">DERIVADA DE f(x) = arcsin(x)</strong></p>\n  <p>La derivada del arco seno es:</p>\n  <p style=\"text-align: center;\">\\[\\frac{d}{dx}(\\arcsin x) = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - x^2}}\\]</p>\n\n  <br>\n  <div style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Ejemplo 1:</strong></div>\n  <div style=\"text-align: center;\">\n    <p>\\[f(x) = \\arcsin x\\]</p>\n    <p>\\[\\frac{d}{dx}(\\arcsin x)\\]</p>\n    <p>\\[f\'(x) = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - x^2}}\\]</p>\n  </div>\n\n  <br>\n  <div style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Ejemplo 2:</strong></div>\n  <div style=\"text-align: center;\">\n    <p>\\[f(x) = \\arcsin(2x)\\]</p>\n    <p>\\[\\frac{d}{dx}(\\arcsin(2x))\\]</p>\n    <p>\\[f\'(x) = \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{1 - (2x)^2}} = \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{1 - 4x^2}}\\]</p>\n  </div>\n</div>\n\n<!-- TEOREMA 2: f(x) = arccos(x) -->\n<div style=\"background-color: #f5f5f5; padding: 15px; margin-bottom: 20px;\">\n  <p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong style=\"color: #0066cc;\">DERIVADA DE f(x) = arccos(x)</strong></p>\n  <p>La derivada del arco coseno es:</p>\n  <p style=\"text-align: center;\">\\[\\frac{d}{dx}(\\arccos x) = -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - x^2}}\\]</p>\n\n  <br>\n  <div style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Ejemplo 1:</strong></div>\n  <div style=\"text-align: center;\">\n    <p>\\[f(x) = \\arccos x\\]</p>\n    <p>\\[\\frac{d}{dx}(\\arccos x)\\]</p>\n    <p>\\[f\'(x) = -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - x^2}}\\]</p>\n  </div>\n\n  <br>\n  <div style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Ejemplo 2:</strong></div>\n  <div style=\"text-align: center;\">\n    <p>\\[f(x) = \\arccos(3x)\\]</p>\n    <p>\\[\\frac{d}{dx}(\\arccos(3x))\\]</p>\n    <p>\\[f\'(x) = -\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{1 - 9x^2}}\\]</p>\n  </div>\n</div>\n\n<!-- TEOREMA 3: f(x) = arctan(x) -->\n<div style=\"background-color: #e6f0ff; padding: 15px; margin-bottom: 20px;\">\n  <p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong style=\"color: #0066cc;\">DERIVADA DE f(x) = arctan(x)</strong></p>\n  <p>La derivada del arco tangente es:</p>\n  <p style=\"text-align: center;\">\\[\\frac{d}{dx}(\\arctan x) = \\frac{1}{1 + x^2}\\]</p>\n\n  <br>\n  <div style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Ejemplo 1:</strong></div>\n  <div style=\"text-align: center;\">\n    <p>\\[f(x) = \\arctan x\\]</p>\n    <p>\\[\\frac{d}{dx}(\\arctan x)\\]</p>\n    <p>\\[f\'(x) = \\frac{1}{1 + x^2}\\]</p>\n  </div>\n\n  <br>\n  <div style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Ejemplo 2:</strong></div>\n  <div style=\"text-align: center;\">\n    <p>\\[f(x) = \\arctan(5x)\\]</p>\n    <p>\\[\\frac{d}{dx}(\\arctan(5x))\\]</p>\n    <p>\\[f\'(x) = \\frac{5}{1 + (5x)^2} = \\frac{5}{1 + 25x^2}\\]</p>\n  </div>\n</div>\n\n<!-- TEOREMA 4: f(x) = arccot(x) -->\n<div style=\"background-color: #f5f5f5; padding: 15px; margin-bottom: 20px;\">\n  <p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong style=\"color: #0066cc;\">DERIVADA DE f(x) = arccot(x)</strong></p>\n  <p>La derivada del arco cotangente es:</p>\n  <p style=\"text-align: center;\">\\[\\frac{d}{dx}(\\arccot x) = -\\frac{1}{1 + x^2}\\]</p>\n\n  <br>\n  <div style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Ejemplo 1:</strong></div>\n  <div style=\"text-align: center;\">\n    <p>\\[f(x) = \\arccot x\\]</p>\n    <p>\\[\\frac{d}{dx}(\\arccot x)\\]</p>\n    <p>\\[f\'(x) = -\\frac{1}{1 + x^2}\\]</p>\n  </div>\n\n  <br>\n  <div style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Ejemplo 2:</strong></div>\n  <div style=\"text-align: center;\">\n    <p>\\[f(x) = \\arccot(2x)\\]</p>\n    <p>\\[\\frac{d}{dx}(\\arccot(2x))\\]</p>\n    <p>\\[f\'(x) = -\\frac{2}{1 + (2x)^2} = -\\frac{2}{1 + 4x^2}\\]</p>\n  </div>\n</div>\n\n<!-- TEOREMA 5: f(x) = arcsec(x) -->\n<div style=\"background-color: #e6f0ff; padding: 15px; margin-bottom: 20px;\">\n  <p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong style=\"color: #0066cc;\">DERIVADA DE f(x) = arcsec(x)</strong></p>\n  <p>La derivada del arco secante es:</p>\n  <p style=\"text-align: center;\">\\[\\frac{d}{dx}(\\arcsec x) = \\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{x^2 - 1}}\\]</p>\n\n  <br>\n  <div style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Ejemplo 1:</strong></div>\n  <div style=\"text-align: center;\">\n    <p>\\[f(x) = \\arcsec x\\]</p>\n    <p>\\[\\frac{d}{dx}(\\arcsec x)\\]</p>\n    <p>\\[f\'(x) = \\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{x^2 - 1}}\\]</p>\n  </div>\n\n  <br>\n  <div style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Ejemplo 2:</strong></div>\n  <div style=\"text-align: center;\">\n    <p>\\[f(x) = \\arcsec(3x)\\]</p>\n    <p>\\[\\frac{d}{dx}(\\arcsec(3x))\\]</p>\n    <p>\\[f\'(x) = \\frac{3}{|3x|\\sqrt{(3x)^2 - 1}} = \\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{9x^2 - 1}}\\]</p>\n  </div>\n</div>\n\n<!-- TEOREMA 6: f(x) = arccsc(x) -->\n<div style=\"background-color: #f5f5f5; padding: 15px; margin-bottom: 20px;\">\n  <p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong style=\"color: #0066cc;\">DERIVADA DE f(x) = arccsc(x)</strong></p>\n  <p>La derivada del arco cosecante es:</p>\n  <p style=\"text-align: center;\">\\[\\frac{d}{dx}(\\arccsc x) = -\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{x^2 - 1}}\\]</p>\n\n  <br>\n  <div style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Ejemplo 1:</strong></div>\n  <div style=\"text-align: center;\">\n    <p>\\[f(x) = \\arccsc x\\]</p>\n    <p>\\[\\frac{d}{dx}(\\arccsc x)\\]</p>\n    <p>\\[f\'(x) = -\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{x^2 - 1}}\\]</p>\n  </div>\n\n  <br>\n  <div style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Ejemplo 2:</strong></div>\n  <div style=\"text-align: center;\">\n    <p>\\[f(x) = \\arccsc(4x)\\]</p>\n    <p>\\[\\frac{d}{dx}(\\arccsc(4x))\\]</p>\n    <p>\\[f\'(x) = -\\frac{4}{|4x|\\sqrt{(4x)^2 - 1}} = -\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{16x^2 - 1}}\\]</p>\n  </div>\n</div>\n\n<div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: center; margin: 20px 0;\">\n  <iframe width=\"560\" height=\"315\" \n    src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/RB5E2qNtgA0\" \n    title=\"Derivadas de funciones trigonométricas inversas | Video educativo\" \n    frameborder=\"0\" \n    allow=\"accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share\" \n    referrerpolicy=\"strict-origin-when-cross-origin\" \n    allowfullscreen>\n  </iframe>\n</div>\n\n<!-- REFERENCIAS -->\n<br>\n<p><strong>Referencias:</strong></p>\n<ul style=\"list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;\">\n  <li>Stewart, J. (2013). <em>Cálculo: Trascendentes tempranas</em> (7ª ed.). Cengage Learning.</li>\n  <li>Larson, R., & Hostetler, R. P. (2006). <em>Cálculo y geometría analítica</em> (8ª ed.). McGraw-Hill.</li>\n  <li>Paul’s Online Math Notes. (n.d.). <em>Calculus I – Derivatives of Inverse Trig Functions</em>. Lamar University. Recuperado de:  \n    <a href=\"https://tutorial.math.lamar.edu/Classes/CalcI/DiffInverseTrig.aspx\" target=\"_blank\">\n      https://tutorial.math.lamar.edu/Classes/CalcI/DiffInverseTrig.aspx\n    </a>\n  </li>\n</ul>','hybrid','','2025-04-15 15:26:45','2025-10-27 19:53:26'),
(77,'C.D_M.3.3.0.4. Teoremas para calcular la derivada de una función exponenciales.','C.D_M.3.3.0.4. Derivada Expone',27,5,1,0,'<!-- TÍTULO PRINCIPAL -->\n<div style=\"background-color: #e6f0ff; border: 2px solid #3399ff; padding: 10px; text-align: center; margin-bottom: 20px;\">\n  <strong style=\"color: #0066cc;\">C.D_M.3.3.0.4. TEOREMAS PARA CALCULAR LA DERIVADA DE UNA FUNCIÓN EXPONENCIAL</strong>\n</div>\n\n<div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: center; margin: 20px 0;\">\n  <iframe width=\"560\" height=\"315\" \n    src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/NEngbw1v56c?si=FmGh2NUs0Qu6cYhN\" \n    title=\"YouTube video player\" \n    frameborder=\"0\" \n    allow=\"accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share\" \n    referrerpolicy=\"strict-origin-when-cross-origin\" \n    allowfullscreen>\n  </iframe>\n</div>\n\n<!-- TEOREMA 1: f(x) = e^x -->\n<div style=\"background-color: #e6f0ff; padding: 15px; margin-bottom: 20px;\">\n  <p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong style=\"color: #0066cc;\">DERIVADA DE f(x) = e^x</strong></p>\n  <p>La derivada de la exponencial natural es:</p>\n  <p style=\"text-align: center;\">\\[\\frac{d}{dx}(e^x) = e^x\\]</p>\n\n  <br>\n  <div style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Ejemplo 1:</strong></div>\n  <div style=\"text-align: center;\">\n    <p>\\[f(x) = e^x\\]</p>\n    <p>\\[\\frac{d}{dx}(e^x)\\]</p>\n    <p>\\[f\'(x) = e^x\\]</p>\n  </div>\n\n  <br>\n  <div style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Ejemplo 2:</strong></div>\n  <div style=\"text-align: center;\">\n    <p>\\[f(x) = 5e^x\\]</p>\n    <p>\\[\\frac{d}{dx}(5e^x)\\]</p>\n    <p>\\[f\'(x) = 5e^x\\]</p>\n  </div>\n</div>\n\n<!-- TEOREMA 2: f(x) = a^x -->\n<div style=\"background-color: #f5f5f5; padding: 15px; margin-bottom: 20px;\">\n  <p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong style=\"color: #0066cc;\">DERIVADA DE f(x) = a^x</strong></p>\n  <p>Para una base constante <em>a &gt; 0</em>, se cumple:</p>\n  <p style=\"text-align: center;\">\\[\\frac{d}{dx}(a^x) = a^x \\ln(a)\\]</p>\n\n  <br>\n  <div style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Ejemplo 1:</strong></div>\n  <div style=\"text-align: center;\">\n    <p>\\[f(x) = 2^x\\]</p>\n    <p>\\[\\frac{d}{dx}(2^x)\\]</p>\n    <p>\\[f\'(x) = 2^x \\ln(2)\\]</p>\n  </div>\n\n  <br>\n  <div style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Ejemplo 2:</strong></div>\n  <div style=\"text-align: center;\">\n    <p>\\[f(x) = 10^x\\]</p>\n    <p>\\[\\frac{d}{dx}(10^x)\\]</p>\n    <p>\\[f\'(x) = 10^x \\ln(10)\\]</p>\n  </div>\n</div>\n\n<!-- TEOREMA 3: f(x) = e^{g(x)} -->\n<div style=\"background-color: #e6f0ff; padding: 15px; margin-bottom: 20px;\">\n  <p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong style=\"color: #0066cc;\">DERIVADA DE UNA EXPONENCIAL COMPUESTA (tipo e^{g(x)})</strong></p>\n  <p>Si la función está compuesta como <em>f(x) = e<sup>g(x)</sup></em>, entonces:</p>\n  <p style=\"text-align: center;\">\\[\\frac{d}{dx}(e^{g(x)}) = e^{g(x)} \\cdot g\'(x)\\]</p>\n\n  <br>\n  <div style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Ejemplo 1:</strong></div>\n  <div style=\"text-align: center;\">\n    <p>\\[f(x) = e^{x^2}\\]</p>\n    <p>\\[\\frac{d}{dx}(e^{x^2})\\]</p>\n    <p>\\[f\'(x) = e^{x^2} \\cdot 2x\\]</p>\n  </div>\n\n  <br>\n  <div style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Ejemplo 2:</strong></div>\n  <div style=\"text-align: center;\">\n    <p>\\[f(x) = e^{\\sin x}\\]</p>\n    <p>\\[\\frac{d}{dx}(e^{\\sin x})\\]</p>\n    <p>\\[f\'(x) = e^{\\sin x} \\cdot \\cos x\\]</p>\n  </div>\n</div>\n\n<!-- TEOREMA 4: f(x) = a^{g(x)} -->\n<div style=\"background-color: #f5f5f5; padding: 15px; margin-bottom: 20px;\">\n  <p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong style=\"color: #0066cc;\">DERIVADA DE UNA EXPONENCIAL COMPUESTA (tipo a^{g(x)})</strong></p>\n  <p>Si la función tiene base <em>a</em> y está compuesta como <em>f(x) = a<sup>g(x)</sup></em>, entonces:</p>\n  <p style=\"text-align: center;\">\\[\\frac{d}{dx}(a^{g(x)}) = a^{g(x)} \\cdot \\ln(a) \\cdot g\'(x)\\]</p>\n\n  <br>\n  <div style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Ejemplo 1:</strong></div>\n  <div style=\"text-align: center;\">\n    <p>\\[f(x) = 3^{x^3}\\]</p>\n    <p>\\[\\frac{d}{dx}(3^{x^3})\\]</p>\n    <p>\\[f\'(x) = 3^{x^3} \\cdot \\ln(3) \\cdot 3x^2\\]</p>\n  </div>\n\n  <br>\n  <div style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Ejemplo 2:</strong></div>\n  <div style=\"text-align: center;\">\n    <p>\\[f(x) = 5^{\\tan x}\\]</p>\n    <p>\\[\\frac{d}{dx}(5^{\\tan x})\\]</p>\n    <p>\\[f\'(x) = 5^{\\tan x} \\cdot \\ln(5) \\cdot \\sec^2 x\\]</p>\n  </div>\n</div>\n\n<!-- TEOREMA 5: f(x) = u(x)^{v(x)} -->\n<div style=\"background-color: #e6f0ff; padding: 15px; margin-bottom: 20px;\">\n  <p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong style=\"color: #0066cc;\">DERIVADA DE f(x) = u(x)^{v(x)}</strong></p>\n  <p>Usamos logaritmos para derivar funciones del tipo potencia variable:</p>\n  <p style=\"text-align: center;\">\\[\\frac{d}{dx}(u(x)^{v(x)}) = u(x)^{v(x)} \\left[ v\'(x) \\ln(u(x)) + v(x) \\cdot \\frac{u\'(x)}{u(x)} \\right]\\]</p>\n\n  <br>\n  <div style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Ejemplo 1:</strong></div>\n  <div style=\"text-align: center;\">\n    <p>\\[f(x) = x^{\\sin x}\\]</p>\n    <p>\\[\\frac{d}{dx}(x^{\\sin x})\\]</p>\n    <p>\\[f\'(x) = x^{\\sin x} \\left[ \\cos x \\ln x + \\frac{\\sin x}{x} \\right]\\]</p>\n  </div>\n\n  <br>\n  <div style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Ejemplo 2:</strong></div>\n  <div style=\"text-align: center;\">\n    <p>\\[f(x) = (x^2 + 1)^{\\tan x}\\]</p>\n    <p>\\[\\frac{d}{dx}((x^2 + 1)^{\\tan x})\\]</p>\n    <p>\\[f\'(x) = (x^2 + 1)^{\\tan x} \\left[ \\sec^2 x \\ln(x^2 + 1) + \\tan x \\cdot \\frac{2x}{x^2 + 1} \\right]\\]</p>\n  </div>\n</div>\n\n<!-- REFERENCIAS -->\n<br>\n<p><strong>Referencias:</strong></p>\n<ul style=\"list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;\">\n  <li>\n    Stewart, J. (2013). <em>Cálculo: Trascendentes tempranas</em> (7ª ed.). Cengage Learning.\n  </li>\n  <li>\n    Larson, R., & Hostetler, R. P. (2006). <em>Cálculo y geometría analítica</em> (8ª ed.). McGraw-Hill.\n  </li>\n  <li>\n    Apostol, T. M. (1967). <em>Calculus, Volume I: One-variable calculus, with an introduction to linear algebra</em> (2ª ed.). Wiley.\n  </li>\n  <li>\n    MIT OpenCourseWare. (n.d.). <em>Single Variable Calculus</em>. Massachusetts Institute of Technology. Recuperado de:  \n    <a href=\"https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/mathematics/18-01sc-single-variable-calculus-fall-2010/\" target=\"_blank\">\n      https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/mathematics/18-01sc-single-variable-calculus-fall-2010/\n    </a>\n  </li>\n  <li>\n    Paul’s Online Math Notes. (n.d.). <em>Calculus I – Derivatives</em>. Lamar University. Recuperado de:  \n    <a href=\"https://tutorial.math.lamar.edu/Classes/CalcI/DerivativeIntro.aspx\" target=\"_blank\">\n      https://tutorial.math.lamar.edu/Classes/CalcI/DerivativeIntro.aspx\n    </a>\n  </li>\n</ul>','hybrid','','2025-04-15 15:26:25','2025-10-15 22:36:46'),
(78,'C.D_M.3.3.0.5. Teoremas para calcular la derivada de una función logarítmicas.','Derivada Logarítmica',27,6,1,0,'<!-- TÍTULO PRINCIPAL -->\n<div style=\"background-color: #e6f0ff; border: 2px solid #3399ff; padding: 10px; text-align: center; margin-bottom: 20px;\">\n  <strong style=\"color: #0066cc;\">C.D_M.3.3.0.5. TEOREMAS PARA CALCULAR LA DERIVADA DE UNA FUNCIÓN LOGARÍTMICA</strong>\n</div>\n\n<!-- TEOREMA 1: f(x) = ln(x) -->\n<div style=\"background-color: #e6f0ff; padding: 15px; margin-bottom: 20px;\">\n  <p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong style=\"color: #0066cc;\">DERIVADA DE f(x) = ln(x)</strong></p>\n  <p>La derivada del logaritmo natural es:</p>\n  <p style=\"text-align: center;\">\\[\\frac{d}{dx}(\\ln x) = \\frac{1}{x}\\]</p>\n  <div style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Ejemplo 1:</strong></div>\n  <p style=\"text-align: center;\">\\[f(x) = \\ln x \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad f\'(x) = \\frac{1}{x}\\]</p>\n  <div style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Ejemplo 2:</strong></div>\n  <p style=\"text-align: center;\">\\[f(x) = 7\\ln x \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad f\'(x) = \\frac{7}{x}\\]</p>\n</div>\n\n<!-- TEOREMA 2: f(x) = log_a(x) -->\n<div style=\"background-color: #f5f5f5; padding: 15px; margin-bottom: 20px;\">\n  <p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong style=\"color: #0066cc;\">DERIVADA DE f(x) = logₐ(x)</strong></p>\n  <p>La derivada del logaritmo en base \\( a \\) es:</p>\n  <p style=\"text-align: center;\">\\[\\frac{d}{dx}(\\log_a x) = \\frac{1}{x \\ln a}\\]</p>\n  <div style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Ejemplo 1:</strong></div>\n  <p style=\"text-align: center;\">\\[f(x) = \\log_2 x \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad f\'(x) = \\frac{1}{x \\ln 2}\\]</p>\n  <div style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Ejemplo 2:</strong></div>\n  <p style=\"text-align: center;\">\\[f(x) = \\log_{10} x \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad f\'(x) = \\frac{1}{x \\ln 10}\\]</p>\n</div>\n\n<!-- TEOREMA 3: f(x) = ln(g(x)) -->\n<div style=\"background-color: #e6f0ff; padding: 15px; margin-bottom: 20px;\">\n  <p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong style=\"color: #0066cc;\">DERIVADA DE UNA FUNCIÓN LOGARÍTMICA COMPUESTA (tipo ln(g(x)))</strong></p>\n  <p>Si la función está compuesta como <em>f(x) = ln(g(x))</em>, entonces:</p>\n  <p style=\"text-align: center;\">\\[\\frac{d}{dx}(\\ln(g(x))) = \\frac{g\'(x)}{g(x)}\\]</p>\n  <div style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Ejemplo 1:</strong></div>\n  <p style=\"text-align: center;\">\\[f(x) = \\ln(x^2 + 1) \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad f\'(x) = \\frac{2x}{x^2 + 1}\\]</p>\n  <div style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Ejemplo 2:</strong></div>\n  <p style=\"text-align: center;\">\\[f(x) = \\ln(\\sin x) \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad f\'(x) = \\frac{\\cos x}{\\sin x}\\]</p>\n</div>\n\n<!-- TEOREMA 4: f(x) = log_a(g(x)) -->\n<div style=\"background-color: #f5f5f5; padding: 15px; margin-bottom: 20px;\">\n  <p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong style=\"color: #0066cc;\">DERIVADA DE UNA FUNCIÓN LOGARÍTMICA COMPUESTA (tipo logₐ(g(x)))</strong></p>\n  <p>Si la función está compuesta como <em>f(x) = logₐ(g(x))</em>, entonces:</p>\n  <p style=\"text-align: center;\">\\[\\frac{d}{dx}(\\log_a(g(x))) = \\frac{g\'(x)}{g(x) \\ln a}\\]</p>\n  <div style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Ejemplo 1:</strong></div>\n  <p style=\"text-align: center;\">\\[f(x) = \\log_3(x^3 + 1) \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad f\'(x) = \\frac{3x^2}{(x^3 + 1)\\ln 3}\\]</p>\n  <div style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Ejemplo 2:</strong></div>\n  <p style=\"text-align: center;\">\\[f(x) = \\log_5(\\tan x) \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad f\'(x) = \\frac{\\sec^2 x}{\\tan x \\ln 5}\\]</p>\n</div>\n\n<!-- REFERENCIAS -->\n<br>\n<p><strong>Referencias:</strong></p>\n<ul style=\"list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;\">\n  <li>\n    Stewart, J. (2013). <em>Cálculo: Trascendentes tempranas</em> (7ª ed.). Cengage Learning.\n  </li>\n  <li>\n    Larson, R., & Hostetler, R. P. (2006). <em>Cálculo y geometría analítica</em> (8ª ed.). McGraw-Hill.\n  </li>\n  <li>\n    Apostol, T. M. (1967). <em>Calculus, Volume I: One-variable calculus, with an introduction to linear algebra</em> (2ª ed.). Wiley.\n  </li>\n  <li>\n    MIT OpenCourseWare. (n.d.). <em>Single Variable Calculus</em>. Massachusetts Institute of Technology. Recuperado de:  \n    <a href=\"https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/mathematics/18-01sc-single-variable-calculus-fall-2010/\" target=\"_blank\">\n      https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/mathematics/18-01sc-single-variable-calculus-fall-2010/\n    </a>\n  </li>\n  <li>\n    Paul’s Online Math Notes. (n.d.). <em>Calculus I – Derivatives</em>. Lamar University. Recuperado de:  \n    <a href=\"https://tutorial.math.lamar.edu/Classes/CalcI/DerivativeIntro.aspx\" target=\"_blank\">\n      https://tutorial.math.lamar.edu/Classes/CalcI/DerivativeIntro.aspx\n    </a>\n  </li>\n</ul>','hybrid','','2025-04-15 15:26:30','2025-10-05 18:32:24'),
